    "title": "Disney, TikTok partner for content creation sharing deal - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jordan Perkins No media credit provided. ,\n29 minutes ago\n( NewsNation ) — If you have Disney+, you might start seeing TikTok content featured on the popular streaming service.\nThe social media company and entertainment giant have partnered in what they are both calling a “first-of-its-kind” content-sharing deal where TikTok videos from Disney fans will live on both of their streaming platforms.\nThe videos will be on Disney’s Verts , which is a vertical video feed on the Disney+ mobile app. Verts was launched in March. TikTok creators will have access to characters from Marvel, Pixar and Star Wars to create videos with.\nLinkedIn adds ‘seems like AI slop’ button In a news release , Disney said the partnership will “give creators a bigger stage to share what they’ve made, and audiences more to discover on Disney+ every day.” The company has previously said short-form content was something they were “actively leaning into.”\nThe last time Disney partnered with another company was with OpenAI’s Sora , which allowed users of the Sora AI video app to create videos featuring Disney characters, but that partnership ended when the video generator was shut down in March.\nA pilot program for the videos will roll out in the coming months and then spread to other markets. An exact date for when the partnership will start was not clear.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WLNS 6 News.",
